# Registered-evaluation run records (pnpm phase4:run). Tens of megabytes each
# -- heldout-a is ~39 MB -- and fully re-derivable from the dataset plus the
# committed code and artifact. report/SRCLA-REPORT.md and the root
# SRCLA-REPORT.json are the committed outputs; these are the verifiable
# intermediates behind them.
evaluation-heldout-*.json
phase4-run.log

# P36's calibration-era validation sweep (scripts/sweep-hurdle-bound.ts). Local
# output; commit deae8408's message records its go/no-go result.
/evaluation-sweep-p36-*.json

# The retired evaluation-v2 harness that produced every report before
# phase4:run (see CLAUDE.md). Kept locally, never tracked.
/quarantine/evaluation-v2/

# Scored-grid sidecars from `pnpm phase4:freeze` (see scripts/freeze-artifact.ts).
#
# DELIBERATE (P18/M2): the REGISTERED artifact's sidecar is COMMITTED as
# evidence. It is ~110 KB, it is the only record of how the registered
# selection was reached -- every per-term IQR, every candidate's normalized
# z-scores and its realised decision score -- and reproducing it costs a
# ~75-minute sweep. A sidecar written beside any OTHER artifact path is
# iteration output and is not evidence of anything registered.
config/*.grid.json
!config/registered-artifact.grid.json

# The P18 selection sweep whose numbers the Task 7 report quotes (winner, the
# per-term IQR table, the -20.785 decomposition, the per-horizon churn
# figures). Produced by scripts/freeze-artifact.ts over the calibration era at
# the registered stride of 12, 4,638 s. It is NOT the registered artifact's
# sidecar -- config/registered-artifact.json still carries the pre-P18
# selection -- so it is named for the sweep rather than for an artifact it
# does not describe. Committed for the same reason as above: it is the only
# record of those numbers and reproducing it costs ~77 minutes.
#
# Two sweeps produced it. The first (commit 6f2ad24f) is what the report's
# numbers were read from; this file is the second (commit 9a30ec68), which
# adds the `foregoneEdge` and `constantTerms` diagnostics and reproduces every
# loss quantity of the first EXACTLY -- same winner, same total to all digits,
# same seven IQRs. That equality is itself the check that the diagnostics do
# not perturb the ranking.
!config/p18-selection-grid.json
